{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc | sed -n '1,900p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.remote-test\n     2\t  \"The slice 8 acceptance row\n     3\t   (`docs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md` slice 8;\n     4\t   `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` S7.4.3, S7.5.3, S7.11.1\n     5\t   'Reflection acceptance'): a REAL machine parked through the engine\n     6\t   on a `:stream-next` wait migrates with a kept cursor and resumes\n     7\t   equivalently in a fresh engine state through a reflection; forced\n     8\t   eviction yields `gap` with the source's own recovery cursor; a\n     9\t   kept cursor that cannot survive the channel codec refuses the lift\n    10\t   before any cell is published; a source `serve!` refuses is\n    11\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied`; an `attach!` that answers gone is\n    12\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the stream at lower. Cursor cells are\n    13\t   minted and remapped across a whole frame set: two waiters on one\n    14\t   engine cell lift to one UCF cell and lower back shared, and\n    15\t   independent cells at one position stay independent (S7.5.3). The\n    16\t   remaining S7.4.3 variants -- `:put`, `:ffi`, `:ffi-request`,\n    17\t   `:link-request`, `:link-response`, `:install` -- round-trip\n    18\t   through stub `serve!`/`attach!` callbacks over the engine's own\n    19\t   wait-set shapes, since their proof is the shape of the bridge, not\n    20\t   the transport. The lowered waits the engine resolves at its own\n    21\t   fixed resource keys resume there for real: a retained\n    22\t   `:link-request` migrates and the engine's own poll retries it and\n    23\t   resumes on the response read at the fixed link keys; a retained\n    24\t   FFI request migrates, its retry appends at the fixed call-in key,\n    25\t   and the restored response wait -- `semantic-restore` parks it on\n    26\t   the receiver's fixed local call-out keys -- receives the retried\n    27\t   response the route cell carried.\"\n    28\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    29\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    30\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n    31\t            [dao.stream.remote :as remote]\n    32\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n    33\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    34\t            [yin.vm.linearize :as linearize]\n    35\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n    36\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n    37\t            [yin.vm.ucf.remote :as ucf.remote]))\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t;; =============================================================================\n    41\t;; The toy: two in-process ring buffers as the channel (as\n    42\t;; dao.stream.remote-test), with a served-table `serve!` on top\n    43\t;; =============================================================================\n    44\t\n    45\t(defn- ring\n    46\t  [capacity]\n    47\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n    48\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer\n    49\t                         :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity capacity})))\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(defn- toy\n    53\t  []\n    54\t  (let [ab (ring 64)\n    55\t        ba (ring 64)\n    56\t        cd {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n    57\t            :dao.stream/identity \"ucf-remote-toy\"}]\n    58\t    {:channel cd, :ab ab, :ba ba,\n    59\t     :a-end {:reader ba, :writer ab},\n    60\t     :b-end {:reader ab, :writer ba}}))\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\t(defn- served-peer\n    64\t  [t]\n    65\t  {:table (atom {})\n    66\t   :b-reader (:reader (:b-end t))\n    67\t   :b-writer (:writer (:b-end t))\n    68\t   :mirror (atom (:dao.stream/cursor\n    69\t                   (stream/cursor (:reader (:b-end t)) :dao.stream/oldest)))})\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\t(defn- serve-mirror!\n    73\t  \"One mirror step over everything pending on the toy's request\n    74\t   buffer.\"\n    75\t  [peer]\n    76\t  (swap! (:mirror peer)\n    77\t         #(remote/mirror-step @(:table peer) (:b-reader peer) %\n    78\t                              (:b-writer peer))))\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t(defn- server\n    82\t  \"The exporter's `serve!` (dao.stream.remote.md S2.3): assigns a\n    83\t   stable identity to `h`, entering it in the peer's table under\n    84\t   `chan`, if it is not already served. The served surface defaults\n    85\t   to reader only; a stream the remote writes through -- a link\n    86\t   request stream the lowered retry appends to, a call-in stream the\n    87\t   retried FFI request lands on -- is served with the writer surface\n    88\t   too.\"\n    89\t  ([peer chan] (server peer chan #{:reader}))\n    90\t  ([peer chan surfaces]\n    91\t   (fn [h]\n    92\t     (if-let [existing (some (fn [[id e]] (when (= h (:handle e)) id))\n    93\t                             @(:table peer))]\n    94\t       {:dao.stream/identity existing, :dao.stream/channel chan}\n    95\t       (let [id (str (gensym \"seg\"))]\n    96\t         (swap! (:table peer) assoc id {:handle h, :surface surfaces})\n    97\t         {:dao.stream/identity id, :dao.stream/channel chan})))))\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\t(defn- attacher\n   101\t  [t]\n   102\t  (remote/attacher\n   103\t    {:dao.stream.remote/channels {(:channel t) (:a-end t)}}))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t;; =============================================================================\n   107\t;; The emitter side: a real machine parked through the engine\n   108\t;; =============================================================================\n   109\t\n   110\t(def ^:private secret\n   111\t  \"The capability secret the test composition gives its machines.\"\n   112\t  \"yin.vm.ucf.remote-test/capability-secret\")\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\t(defn- make-ring-stream\n   116\t  \"The ring-buffer `:make-stream` this composition gives its\n   117\t   machines -- `yin.vm.test-utils`'s choice, at test scale.\"\n   118\t  [capacity]\n   119\t  (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer\n   120\t                       :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity capacity}))\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn- new-machine\n   124\t  \"A fresh semantic machine over that composition.\"\n   125\t  []\n   126\t  (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream make-ring-stream\n   127\t                       :capability-secret secret}))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(def ^:private load-ast\n   131\t  \"The trusted fresh path: the AST linearizer behind the code loader.\"\n   132\t  (vm/fresh-code-loader (linearize/ast-loader semantic/vm-load-program)\n   133\t                        vm/ast-contract))\n   134\t\n   135\t\n   136\t(defn- var-ref\n   137\t  [n]\n   138\t  {:type :variable, :name n})\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   141\t(defn- let1\n   142\t  \"`((fn [param] body) init)`.\"\n   143\t  [param init body]\n   144\t  {:type :application,\n   145\t   :operator {:type :lambda, :params [param], :body body},\n   146\t   :operands [init]})\n   147\t\n   148\t\n   149\t(defn- reader-datoms\n   150\t  \"Make a stream of `capacity`, mint a cursor on it, read one value.\"\n   151\t  [capacity]\n   152\t  (vm/ast->datoms\n   153\t    (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer capacity}\n   154\t          {:type :stream/next,\n   155\t           :source {:type :stream/cursor, :source (var-ref 's)}})))\n   156\t\n   157\t\n   158\t(defn- parked-reader\n   159\t  \"A real machine parked through the engine on a `:stream-next` wait\n   160\t   over a fresh ring buffer: the code datoms, the parked VM, its\n   161\t   wait-set entry, and the stream handle the entry polls.\"\n   162\t  [capacity]\n   163\t  (let [datoms (reader-datoms capacity)\n   164\t        parked (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) datoms))\n   165\t        entry (first (:wait-set parked))]\n   166\t    [datoms parked entry\n   167\t     (get (:resources parked) (:stream-id entry))]))\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\t(defn- lit\n   171\t  [v]\n   172\t  {:type :literal, :value v})\n   173\t\n   174\t\n   175\t(defn- one-slot-stream\n   176\t  \"A stream that answers `full` while one value sits in it -- the one\n   177\t   append outcome a ring buffer never gives (a ringbuffer evicts),\n   178\t   without which no request stays retained. Reading the value frees\n   179\t   the slot. The descriptor answers ok, so the reflection's attach\n   180\t   probe is answerable.\"\n   181\t  [identity]\n   182\t  (let [slot (atom :empty)]\n   183\t    (reify\n   184\t      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   185\t      (descriptor\n   186\t        [_]\n   187\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n   188\t         :dao.stream/identity identity,\n   189\t         :dao.stream/descriptor\n   190\t         {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel,\n   191\t          :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n   192\t\n   193\t\n   194\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   195\t\n   196\t      (cursor\n   197\t        [_ _anchor]\n   198\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok, :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n   199\t\n   200\t      (next\n   201\t        [_ cursor]\n   202\t        (if (and (= 0 cursor) (not= :empty @slot))\n   203\t          (let [v @slot]\n   204\t            (reset! slot :empty)\n   205\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n   206\t             :dao.stream/value v, :dao.stream/cursor 1})\n   207\t          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))\n   208\t\n   209\t\n   210\t      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   211\t\n   212\t      (append!\n   213\t        [_ v]\n   214\t        (if (not= :empty @slot)\n   215\t          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/full}\n   216\t          (do (reset! slot v)\n   217\t              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))))))\n   218\t\n   219\t\n   220\t(defn- requirer-datoms\n   221\t  \"The datoms of `(require name)` -- the effectful primitive whose\n   222\t   miss parks mid-link (`module/require-handler`).\"\n   223\t  [name]\n   224\t  (vm/ast->datoms\n   225\t    {:type :application,\n   226\t     :operator {:type :variable, :name 'require},\n   227\t     :operands [(lit name)]}))\n   228\t\n   229\t\n   230\t(defn- linking-machine\n   231\t  \"A fresh semantic machine composed over a link pair, the module\n   232\t   kernel's own composition keys (`yin.vm.linker.md` S6.1).\"\n   233\t  [request response]\n   234\t  (semantic/create-vm\n   235\t    {:make-stream make-ring-stream,\n   236\t     :capability-secret secret,\n   237\t     :modules (module/default-registry),\n   238\t     :link-request request,\n   239\t     :link-response response}))\n   240\t\n   241\t\n   242\t(defn- linked-machine\n   243\t  \"A fresh semantic machine whose registry already holds `name` as a\n   244\t   host module: `settle`'s own linked-meanwhile answer, no install\n   245\t   child needed.\"\n   246\t  [name]\n   247\t  (semantic/create-vm\n   248\t    {:make-stream make-ring-stream,\n   249\t     :capability-secret secret,\n   250\t     :modules (module/register-host-module\n   251\t                (module/default-registry) name\n   252\t                {'answer 42}\n   253\t                {'answer (vm/primitive-profile 'answer :pure [0]\n   254\t                                               #{} :none)})}))\n   255\t\n   256\t\n   257\t(defn- parked-requirer\n   258\t  \"A real machine parked mid-link by a require: the request stream\n   259\t   holds one warm-up value, so `require-handler`'s append refuses\n   260\t   with full and the entry keeps its envelope -- a retained\n   261\t   `:link-request`, the engine's own fields, registers and pair.\"\n   262\t  [name]\n   263\t  (let [request (one-slot-stream \"link-request\")\n   264\t        response (ring 64)\n   265\t        _ (stream/append! request :warmed)\n   266\t        datoms (requirer-datoms name)\n   267\t        parked (vm/run (load-ast (linking-machine request response)\n   268\t                                 datoms))\n   269\t        entry (first (:wait-set parked))]\n   270\t    [datoms parked entry request response]))\n   271\t\n   272\t\n   273\t(defn- call-node\n   274\t  \"A `:dao.stream.apply/call` of `op` with one literal argument.\"\n   275\t  [op arg]\n   276\t  {:type :dao.stream.apply/call, :op op,\n   277\t   :operands [(lit arg)]})\n   278\t\n   279\t\n   280\t(defn- then\n   281\t  \"`((fn [_] second) first)`: first for its effect, then second.\"\n   282\t  [first-ast second-ast]\n   283\t  {:type :application,\n   284\t   :operator {:type :lambda, :params ['_], :body second-ast},\n   285\t   :operands [first-ast]})\n   286\t\n   287\t\n   288\t(defn- calling-machine\n   289\t  \"A fresh semantic machine composed over an FFI call pair, under the\n   290\t   engine's own fixed pair keys (`vm.cljc`'s `:call-in`/`:call-out`\n   291\t   composition keys). `bridge` is the machine's own handler map for\n   292\t   calls that arrive on that pair.\"\n   293\t  [call-in call-out bridge]\n   294\t  (semantic/create-vm\n   295\t    {:make-stream make-ring-stream,\n   296\t     :capability-secret secret,\n   297\t     :call-in call-in,\n   298\t     :call-out call-out,\n   299\t     :bridge bridge}))\n   300\t\n   301\t\n   302\t(defn- parked-caller\n   303\t  \"A real machine parked on a retained FFI request: the call-in\n   304\t   stream holds one warm-up value, so the first call's put refuses\n   305\t   with full and the entry keeps the request -- the engine's own\n   306\t   `:request-sent` shape, the pair under its fixed resource keys.\n   307\t   `ast` may call again after the first call, so a resume can watch\n   308\t   where a future call routes.\"\n   309\t  [ast]\n   310\t  (let [call-in (one-slot-stream \"call-in\")\n   311\t        call-out (ring 8)\n   312\t        _ (stream/append! call-in :warmed)\n   313\t        datoms (vm/ast->datoms ast)\n   314\t        parked (vm/run (load-ast (calling-machine call-in call-out nil)\n   315\t                                 datoms))\n   316\t        entry (first (:wait-set parked))]\n   317\t    [datoms parked entry call-in call-out]))\n   318\t\n   319\t\n   320\t(defn- registers-of\n   321\t  \"The register payload a parked entry carries.\"\n   322\t  [entry]\n   323\t  (select-keys entry [:segment :pc :env :stack :k]))\n   324\t\n   325\t\n   326\t(defn- quiesced-receiver\n   327\t  \"The fresh engine state a lower installs into: a real machine over\n   328\t   the same code image, quiesced, holding the lowered resource table\n   329\t   and the lowered wait-set entry -- nothing of the emitter's state\n   330\t   but the code image and the registers the entry carries.\"\n   331\t  ([datoms lowered] (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered (new-machine)))\n   332\t  ([datoms lowered machine]\n   333\t   (assoc (load-ast machine datoms)\n   334\t          :control nil, :k nil,\n   335\t          :value :yin/blocked, :blocked? true, :halted? false,\n   336\t          :wait-set [(:entry lowered)],\n   337\t          :resources (:resources lowered))))\n   338\t\n   339\t\n   340\t(defn- cursor-entries\n   341\t  \"The cursor entries of a lowered resource table: maps keyed by the\n   342\t   UCF cell ids, each carrying its stream id and kept cursor.\"\n   343\t  [table]\n   344\t  (into {} (filter (fn [[_ v]] (and (map? v) (contains? v :stream-id))))\n   345\t        table))\n   346\t\n   347\t\n   348\t;; =============================================================================\n   349\t;; The acceptance row: a real parked machine migrates and resumes\n   350\t;; =============================================================================\n   351\t\n   352\t(deftest migrates-a-real-parked-machine-and-resumes\n   353\t  (let [t (toy)\n   354\t        peer (served-peer t)\n   355\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t))\n   356\t        attach! (attacher t)\n   357\t        [datoms parked entry src] (parked-reader 4)\n   358\t        cid (:id (:cursor-ref entry))\n   359\t        sid (:stream-id entry)\n   360\t        kept (get-in parked [:resources cid :cursor])\n   361\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! (:resources parked) entry)\n   362\t        lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   363\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\n   364\t                                          (registers-of entry))\n   365\t        receiver (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered)]\n   366\t    (testing \"the machine parked through the engine\"\n   367\t      (is (vm/blocked? parked))\n   368\t      (is (= :next (:reason entry)))\n   369\t      (is (= :cursor-ref (get-in entry [:cursor-ref :type]))))\n   370\t    (testing \"the lift reads the engine's own wait-set entry\"\n   371\t      (is (= {:yin.k/reason :next, :yin.k/cell :yin.k/c-0}\n   372\t             (:yin.k/pending lifted))\n   373\t          \"the cursor CELL id, S7.5.3 -- not a bare position\")\n   374\t      (is (= kept (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/position]))\n   375\t          \"the cell carries the engine's kept cursor\")\n   376\t      (is (= #{:dao.stream.remote/v1}\n   377\t             (get-in lifted [:yin.k/requires :yin.k/cursor-profiles]))))\n   378\t    (testing \"the lower builds a fresh engine state\"\n   379\t      (let [e (:entry lowered)\n   380\t            rs (:resources lowered)\n   381\t            cid' (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id])\n   382\t            sid' (:stream-id e)]\n   383\t        (is (= (registers-of entry) (registers-of e))\n   384\t            \"the register context rides the lower verbatim\")\n   385\t        (is (not= cid cid'))\n   386\t        (is (not= sid sid'))\n   387\t        (is (not (contains? rs cid)))\n   388\t        (is (not (contains? rs sid)))\n   389\t        (is (= {:stream-id sid', :cursor kept} (get rs cid'))\n   390\t            \"one fresh cursor entry, at the kept position\")\n   391\t        (is (not= src (get rs sid'))\n   392\t            \"the stream entry is a reflection, not the emitter's handle\")\n   393\t        (is (= sid' (get-in rs [cid' :stream-id])))))\n   394\t    (testing \"the emitter's own wait resumes equivalently\"\n   395\t      (stream/append! src \"hello\")\n   396\t      (is (= \"hello\" (vm/value (vm/run parked)))))\n   397\t    (testing \"the migrated wait resumes in the fresh engine state\"\n   398\t      (is (vm/blocked? (vm/run receiver))\n   399\t          \"the reflection answers blocked until the mirror serves\")\n   400\t      (serve-mirror! peer)\n   401\t      (let [done (vm/run receiver)]\n   402\t        (is (vm/halted? done))\n   403\t        (is (= \"hello\" (vm/value done))\n   404\t            \"the source's own value, through the kept cursor\")\n   405\t        (is (empty? (:wait-set done)))))))\n   406\t\n   407\t\n   408\t(deftest forced-eviction-yields-gap-with-the-sources-cursor\n   409\t  (let [t (toy)\n   410\t        peer (served-peer t)\n   411\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t))\n   412\t        attach! (attacher t)\n   413\t        [datoms parked entry src] (parked-reader 2)\n   414\t        cid (:id (:cursor-ref entry))\n   415\t        kept (get-in parked [:resources cid :cursor])\n   416\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! (:resources parked) entry)\n   417\t        lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   418\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\n   419\t                                          (registers-of entry))\n   420\t        cid' (get-in (:entry lowered) [:cursor-ref :id])\n   421\t        receiver (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered)]\n   422\t    (stream/append! src \"hello\")\n   423\t    (doseq [v [\"v1\" \"v2\" \"v3\"]]\n   424\t      (stream/append! src v))\n   425\t    (is (vm/blocked? (vm/run receiver)))\n   426\t    (serve-mirror! peer)\n   427\t    (let [expected (stream/next src kept)\n   428\t          done (vm/run receiver)]\n   429\t      (testing \"the program reads the source's own gap, verbatim\"\n   430\t        (is (= :dao.stream/gap (vm/value done)))\n   431\t        (is (= (:dao.stream/cursor expected)\n   432\t               (get-in done [:resources cid' :cursor]))\n   433\t            \"with the source's own recovery cursor in the cell\"))\n   434\t      (testing \"no replay and no silent skip: the walk continues\n   435\t                from the recovery cursor\"\n   436\t        (let [r (get-in done [:resources (:stream-id (:entry lowered))])\n   437\t              recovery (get-in done [:resources cid' :cursor])]\n   438\t          (is (= :dao.stream/blocked\n   439\t                 (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/next r recovery))))\n   440\t          (serve-mirror! peer)\n   441\t          (let [ok (stream/next r recovery)]\n   442\t            (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome ok)))\n   443\t            (is (= \"v2\" (:dao.stream/value ok)))))))))\n   444\t\n   445\t\n   446\t;; =============================================================================\n   447\t;; The fixed keys: lowered link waits and retained FFI requests\n   448\t;; resume through the engine's own poll and retry paths\n   449\t;; =============================================================================\n   450\t\n   451\t(deftest a-lowered-link-request-retries-and-resumes-through-the-engine\n   452\t  (let [t (toy)\n   453\t        peer (served-peer t)\n   454\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t) #{:reader :writer})\n   455\t        attach! (attacher t)\n   456\t        [datoms parked entry req-src resp-src]\n   457\t        (parked-requirer 'host.the-module)\n   458\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! (:resources parked) entry)\n   459\t        pending (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   460\t        lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! pending\n   461\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\n   462\t                                          (registers-of entry))\n   463\t        e (:entry lowered)\n   464\t        rs (:resources lowered)\n   465\t        receiver (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered\n   466\t                                    (linked-machine 'host.the-module))]\n   467\t    (testing \"the machine parked through the engine, envelope retained\"\n   468\t      (is (vm/blocked? parked))\n   469\t      (is (= :link-request (:reason entry)))\n   470\t      (is (= module/link-request-resource (:request entry)))\n   471\t      (is (= module/link-response-resource (:response entry)))\n   472\t      (is (map? (:envelope entry)) \"the request the retry appends\"))\n   473\t    (testing \"the lower parks the wait where the engine polls\"\n   474\t      (is (= module/link-request-resource (:request e))\n   475\t          \"the retry appends at the engine's fixed request key\")\n   476\t      (is (= module/link-response-resource (:response e))\n   477\t          \"the poll reads at the engine's fixed response key\")\n   478\t      (is (contains? rs (:request e)))\n   479\t      (is (contains? rs (:response e))\n   480\t          \"the pair's reflections stand under the fixed keys\"))\n   481\t    (testing \"the engine's own poll retries and resumes the require\"\n   482\t      ;; the linker answered before the migration: the response sits\n   483\t      ;; on the emitter's response stream, past the kept cursor\n   484\t      (stream/append! resp-src\n   485\t                      {:status :ok,\n   486\t                       :yin.link/id (:link-id entry),\n   487\t                       :manifest {:yin.module/name 'host.the-module}})\n   488\t      (is (vm/blocked? (vm/run receiver))\n   489\t          \"first poll: the envelope is retried, the answer not yet read\")\n   490\t      (let [w0 (:dao.stream/cursor\n   491\t                 (stream/cursor req-src :dao.stream/oldest))]\n   492\t        (is (= :warmed\n   493\t               (:dao.stream/value (stream/next req-src w0)))\n   494\t            \"reading the warm-up frees the slot the retry needs\"))\n   495\t      (serve-mirror! peer)\n   496\t      (let [c0 (:dao.stream/cursor\n   497\t                 (stream/cursor req-src :dao.stream/oldest))\n   498\t            r (stream/next req-src c0)]\n   499\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n   500\t        (is (= (:envelope entry) (:dao.stream/value r))\n   501\t            \"the envelope verbatim, appended via the fixed request key\"))\n   502\t      (let [done (vm/run receiver)]\n   503\t        (is (vm/halted? done))\n   504\t        (is (= 'host.the-module (vm/value done))\n   505\t            \"the require resumes with the module's own value\")\n   506\t        (is (empty? (:wait-set done)))))))\n   507\t\n   508\t\n   509\t(deftest a-retained-ffi-request-migrates-and-the-retry-resumes\n   510\t  (let [t (toy)\n   511\t        peer (served-peer t)\n   512\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t) #{:reader :writer})\n   513\t        attach! (attacher t)\n   514\t        program (then (call-node :op/echo \"hello\")\n   515\t                      (call-node :op/echo \"world\"))\n   516\t        [datoms parked entry call-in-src call-out-src]\n   517\t        (parked-caller program)\n   518\t        kept (get-in parked [:resources vm/call-out-cursor-key :cursor])\n   519\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! (:resources parked) entry)\n   520\t        pending (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   521\t        ;; the resumer's own pair and its own handler, under the fixed\n   522\t        ;; keys: they serve the program's subsequent calls and can\n   523\t        ;; never answer the migrated one\n   524\t        own-call-in (ring 8)\n   525\t        own-call-out (ring 8)\n   526\t        own (calling-machine own-call-in own-call-out\n   527\t                             {:op/echo (constantly \"local!\")})\n   528\t        own-pair (select-keys (:resources own)\n   529\t                              [vm/call-in-stream-key\n   530\t                               vm/call-out-stream-key\n   531\t                               vm/call-out-cursor-key])\n   532\t        lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! pending\n   533\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\n   534\t                                          (registers-of entry)\n   535\t                                          (keys own-pair))\n   536\t        e (:entry lowered)\n   537\t        rs (:resources lowered)\n   538\t        receiver (-> (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered own)\n   539\t                     (update :resources #(merge own-pair %)))\n   540\t        oldest (fn [h]\n   541\t                 (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h :dao.stream/oldest)))\n   542\t        ;; the emitter's bridge answered the migrated call before the\n   543\t        ;; migration: the response sits on the emitter's call-out,\n   544\t        ;; past the kept cursor\n   545\t        _ (stream/append! call-out-src\n   546\t                          (apply2/success-response\n   547\t                            (:call-id entry) \"echo!\"))\n   548\t        ;; phase 1: the sweep retries the retained request through the\n   549\t        ;; carried request reflection, and the restored response wait\n   550\t        ;; polls the carried response route\n   551\t        r1 (vm/run receiver)\n   552\t        wait-a (first (:wait-set r1))\n   553\t        warm-up (stream/next call-in-src (oldest call-in-src))\n   554\t        _ (serve-mirror! peer)\n   555\t        landed (stream/next call-in-src (oldest call-in-src))\n   556\t        ;; phase 2: the carried route delivers the response; the\n   557\t        ;; program's own next call parks on the receiver's local pair\n   558\t        ;; and its own handler answers it there\n   559\t        r2 (vm/run r1)]\n   560\t    (testing \"the machine parked through the engine, request retained\"\n   561\t      (is (vm/blocked? parked))\n   562\t      (is (true? (:request-sent entry)))\n   563\t      (is (= vm/call-in-stream-key (:stream-id entry)))\n   564\t      (is (apply2/request? (:datom entry))))\n   565\t    (testing \"the lift carries both endpoints and the kept response cell\"\n   566\t      (is (contains? pending :yin.k/request))\n   567\t      (is (contains? pending :yin.k/response)\n   568\t          \"both endpoint markers ride beside the retained envelope\")\n   569\t      (is (= :yin.k/c-0 (:yin.k/response-cell pending)))\n   570\t      (is (= (get-in pending [:yin.k/response :dao.stream/identity])\n   571\t             (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/stream\n   572\t                             :dao.stream/identity]))\n   573\t          \"the response endpoint's marker is the route cell's stream\")\n   574\t      (is (= kept\n   575\t             (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/position]))\n   576\t          \"the kept response position\"))\n   577\t    (testing \"the lower allocates fresh keys and carries the route\"\n   578\t      (is (contains? rs (:stream-id e))\n   579\t          \"the retry writes through the carried request reflection\")\n   580\t      (is (not= vm/call-in-stream-key (:stream-id e))\n   581\t          \"never the receiver's own call-in key\")\n   582\t      (is (not (contains? rs vm/call-in-stream-key)))\n   583\t      (is (not (contains? rs vm/call-out-stream-key)))\n   584\t      (is (not (contains? rs vm/call-out-cursor-key))\n   585\t          \"no route is ever installed at a fixed key\")\n   586\t      (is (= (:response-cursor e) (get-in wait-a [:cursor-ref :id]))\n   587\t          \"the restored response wait polls the carried cell's key\")\n   588\t      (is (= (:response-stream e) (:stream-id wait-a))\n   589\t          \"reading the carried response reflection\")\n   590\t      (let [route (get rs (:response-cursor e))]\n   591\t        (is (= kept (:cursor route))\n   592\t            \"at the kept response position\")\n   593\t        (is (= (:response-stream e) (:stream-id route))\n   594\t            \"naming the carried response reflection\")\n   595\t        (is (contains? rs (:response-stream e)))))\n   596\t    (testing \"the retried call is answered on the emitter's pair\"\n   597\t      (is (vm/blocked? r1)\n   598\t          \"first round: the request is retried, the response not yet\n   599\t           read\")\n   600\t      (is (= :warmed (:dao.stream/value warm-up))\n   601\t          \"reading the warm-up freed the slot the retry needed\")\n   602\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome landed)))\n   603\t      (is (= (:datom entry) (:dao.stream/value landed))\n   604\t          \"the retained request verbatim, through the carried request\n   605\t           reflection\")\n   606\t      (is (= \"echo!\"\n   607\t             (apply2/response-ok\n   608\t               (:dao.stream/value\n   609\t                 (stream/next call-out-src (oldest call-out-src)))))\n   610\t          \"the emitter's bridge answered it on the emitter's pair\"))\n   611\t    (testing \"the carried route delivers, and later calls are local\"\n   612\t      (is (vm/halted? r2))\n   613\t      (is (= \"local!\" (vm/value r2))\n   614\t          \"the migrated result came from the emitter's bridge; the\n   615\t           receiver's own handler answered only the program's own next\n   616\t           call\")\n   617\t      (is (not= kept (:cursor (get-in r2 [:resources\n   618\t                                          (:response-cursor e)])))\n   619\t          \"the carried route's cursor advanced: the response was read\n   620\t           through it\")\n   621\t      (is (= [\"world\"]\n   622\t             (apply2/request-args\n   623\t               (:dao.stream/value\n   624\t                 (stream/next own-call-in (oldest own-call-in)))))\n   625\t          \"the subsequent call's request is on the receiver's own\n   626\t           call-in\")\n   627\t      (is (= \"local!\"\n   628\t             (apply2/response-ok\n   629\t               (:dao.stream/value\n   630\t                 (stream/next own-call-out (oldest own-call-out)))))\n   631\t          \"and its answer is on the receiver's own call-out\"))))\n   632\t\n   633\t\n   634\t;; =============================================================================\n   635\t;; Unsatisfied: an unpublishable cursor, a source that cannot be\n   636\t;; served, a gone reflection\n   637\t;; =============================================================================\n   638\t\n   639\t(defn- host-cursor-stream\n   640\t  \"A handle whose cursors hold a host object -- the case\n   641\t   dao.stream.remote.md S2.3 says cannot be served.\"\n   642\t  []\n   643\t  (reify stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   644\t    (descriptor\n   645\t      [_]\n   646\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   647\t       :dao.stream/identity \"host-cursor\"\n   648\t       :dao.stream/descriptor\n   649\t       {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n   650\t        :dao.stream/identity \"host-cursor\"}})\n   651\t\n   652\t\n   653\t    stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   654\t\n   655\t    (cursor\n   656\t      [_ _]\n   657\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   658\t       :dao.stream/cursor {:position 0, :owner (fn [x] x)}})\n   659\t\n   660\t    (next\n   661\t      [_ _]\n   662\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked})))\n   663\t\n   664\t\n   665\t(deftest a-cursor-that-cannot-round-trip-is-refused\n   666\t  (let [t (toy)\n   667\t        peer (served-peer t)\n   668\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t))\n   669\t        s (host-cursor-stream)\n   670\t        resources {:yin/host-stream s,\n   671\t                   :yin/host-cursor\n   672\t                   {:stream-id :yin/host-stream,\n   673\t                    :cursor {:position 0, :owner (fn [x] x)}}}\n   674\t        entry {:reason :next,\n   675\t               :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/host-cursor},\n   676\t               :stream-id :yin/host-stream}\n   677\t        refusal (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! resources entry)]\n   678\t    (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied (:yin.k/status refusal))\n   679\t        \"the profile claim is checked before anything is published\")\n   680\t    (is (= \"host-cursor\" (:dao.stream/identity refusal))\n   681\t        \"naming the stream identity\")\n   682\t    (is (empty? @(:table peer))\n   683\t        \"refused before `serve!` even mints the descriptor\")))\n   684\t\n   685\t\n   686\t(deftest lift-refuses-unsatisfied-when-the-source-cannot-be-served\n   687\t  (let [s (ring 4)]\n   688\t    (stream/append! s \"x\")\n   689\t    (let [c0 (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor s :dao.stream/oldest))\n   690\t          resources {:yin/s s, :yin/c {:stream-id :yin/s, :cursor c0}}\n   691\t          entry {:reason :next,\n   692\t                 :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/c},\n   693\t                 :stream-id :yin/s}\n   694\t          refusal (ucf.remote/lift-pending (constantly nil) resources entry)]\n   695\t      (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied (:yin.k/status refusal))\n   696\t          \"lift refuses before minting the value\")\n   697\t      (is (contains? refusal :dao.stream/identity)\n   698\t          \"naming the stream identity\"))))\n   699\t\n   700\t\n   701\t(deftest lower-refuses-unsatisfied-when-the-reflection-is-gone\n   702\t  (let [attach! (constantly {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n   703\t                             :dao.stream.remote/reason\n   704\t                             :dao.stream.remote/not-found})\n   705\t        marker {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/stream,\n   706\t                :dao.stream/identity \"missing\",\n   707\t                :dao.stream/descriptor\n   708\t                {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote,\n   709\t                 :dao.stream/identity \"missing\",\n   710\t                 :dao.stream/channel\n   711\t                 {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel,\n   712\t                  :dao.stream/identity \"elsewhere\"}}}\n   713\t        pending {:yin.k/reason :next, :yin.k/cell :yin.k/c-0}\n   714\t        cells {:yin.k/c-0 {:yin.k/stream marker, :yin.k/position 0}}\n   715\t        lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! pending cells {})]\n   716\t    (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied (:yin.k/status lowered)))\n   717\t    (is (= \"missing\" (:dao.stream/identity lowered))\n   718\t        \"naming the stream identity\")))\n   719\t\n   720\t\n   721\t;; =============================================================================\n   722\t;; Frame-level cells (S7.5.3): shared and independent\n   723\t;; =============================================================================\n   724\t\n   725\t(defn- stub-serve!\n   726\t  \"A `serve!` that assigns every handle to one identity per handle\n   727\t   under `chan`, with no wire underneath: these variants prove the\n   728\t   bridge's shape, the transport already proven above.\"\n   729\t  [chan]\n   730\t  (let [ids (atom {})]\n   731\t    (fn [h]\n   732\t      (let [id (or (get @ids h)\n   733\t                   (let [n (str (gensym \"seg\"))]\n   734\t                     (swap! ids assoc h n)\n   735\t                     n))]\n   736\t        {:dao.stream/identity id, :dao.stream/channel chan}))))\n   737\t\n   738\t\n   739\t(defn- stub-attach!\n   740\t  \"An `attach!` that answers ok at once with a reflection standing for\n   741\t   the descriptor's identity -- opaque here, since these variants\n   742\t   never poll it.\"\n   743\t  []\n   744\t  (fn [d]\n   745\t    {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n   746\t     :dao.stream/handle [:reflection-of (:dao.stream/identity d)]}))\n   747\t\n   748\t\n   749\t(def ^:private chan\n   750\t  {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel, :dao.stream/identity \"c\"})\n   751\t\n   752\t\n   753\t(deftest shared-cursor-cells-lift-and-lower-shared\n   754\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\n   755\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\n   756\t        [_datoms parked entry _src] (parked-reader 4)\n   757\t        cid (:id (:cursor-ref entry))\n   758\t        ;; a second waiter on the SAME engine cursor cell, as\n   759\t        ;; check-wait-set's shared-cursor co-waiters hold\n   760\t        second (assoc (registers-of entry)\n   761\t                      :reason :next,\n   762\t                      :stream-id (:stream-id entry),\n   763\t                      :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid},\n   764\t                      :pc 42)\n   765\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-frame serve! (:resources parked)\n   766\t                                      [entry second])]\n   767\t    (testing \"two waiters on one engine cell lift to one UCF cell\"\n   768\t      (is (= 1 (count (:yin.k/cells lifted))))\n   769\t      (let [[p1 p2] (:yin.k/pending lifted)]\n   770\t        (is (= (:yin.k/cell p1) (:yin.k/cell p2))\n   771\t            \"both waiters name the one cell\")))\n   772\t    (let [ctxs [(registers-of entry) (registers-of second)]\n   773\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-frame attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   774\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted) ctxs)\n   775\t          [e1 e2] (:entries lowered)\n   776\t          rs (:resources lowered)]\n   777\t      (testing \"and lower back into one shared cursor entry\"\n   778\t        (is (= (get-in e1 [:cursor-ref :id])\n   779\t               (get-in e2 [:cursor-ref :id]))\n   780\t            \"one cell id stands for the one entry\")\n   781\t        (is (= 1 (count (cursor-entries rs)))))\n   782\t      (testing \"each entry keeps its own register context\"\n   783\t        (is (= (:pc entry) (:pc e1)))\n   784\t        (is (= 42 (:pc e2)))))))\n   785\t\n   786\t\n   787\t(deftest independent-cells-at-one-position-stay-independent\n   788\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\n   789\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\n   790\t        s (ring 8)\n   791\t        _ (stream/append! s \"v\")\n   792\t        c0 (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor s :dao.stream/oldest))\n   793\t        resources {:yin/s s,\n   794\t                   :yin/c1 {:stream-id :yin/s, :cursor c0},\n   795\t                   :yin/c2 {:stream-id :yin/s, :cursor c0}}\n   796\t        entry1 {:reason :next,\n   797\t                :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/c1},\n   798\t                :stream-id :yin/s}\n   799\t        entry2 {:reason :next,\n   800\t                :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/c2},\n   801\t                :stream-id :yin/s}\n   802\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-frame serve! resources\n   803\t                                      [entry1 entry2])]\n   804\t    (testing \"two engine cells at one position are two UCF cells\"\n   805\t      (is (= 2 (count (:yin.k/cells lifted)))\n   806\t          \"the aliasing a position-only encoding erases, kept\")\n   807\t      (let [[p1 p2] (:yin.k/pending lifted)]\n   808\t        (is (not= (:yin.k/cell p1) (:yin.k/cell p2)))\n   809\t        (is (= c0 (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells (:yin.k/cell p1)\n   810\t                                  :yin.k/position])))\n   811\t        (is (= c0 (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells (:yin.k/cell p2)\n   812\t                                  :yin.k/position])))))\n   813\t    (let [ctx {:segment 0, :pc 1, :env {}, :stack [], :k []}\n   814\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-frame attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   815\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\n   816\t                                          [ctx ctx])\n   817\t          [e1 e2] (:entries lowered)\n   818\t          rs (:resources lowered)]\n   819\t      (testing \"and lower into two independently advanceable entries\"\n   820\t        (is (not= (get-in e1 [:cursor-ref :id])\n   821\t                  (get-in e2 [:cursor-ref :id])))\n   822\t        (is (= 2 (count (cursor-entries rs))))\n   823\t        (is (= 1 (count (filter vector? (vals rs))))\n   824\t            \"one stream, so the two cells share one reflection\")))))\n   825\t\n   826\t\n   827\t(deftest a-refused-leaf-refuses-the-frame\n   828\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\n   829\t        s (ring 4)\n   830\t        c0 (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor s :dao.stream/oldest))\n   831\t        resources {:yin/s s, :yin/c {:stream-id :yin/s, :cursor c0}}\n   832\t        good {:reason :next,\n   833\t              :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/c},\n   834\t              :stream-id :yin/s}]\n   835\t    (is (= :yin.k/undecodable\n   836\t           (:yin.k/status\n   837\t             (ucf.remote/lift-frame serve! resources\n   838\t                                    [good {:reason :bogus}])))\n   839\t        \"an unrecognized reason is total, S7.5.4\")\n   840\t    (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied\n   841\t           (:yin.k/status\n   842\t             (ucf.remote/lift-frame (constantly nil) resources [good]))))))\n   843\t\n   844\t\n   845\t;; =============================================================================\n   846\t;; The remaining S7.4.3 variants round-trip, over the engine's shapes\n   847\t;; =============================================================================\n   848\t\n   849\t(deftest a-blocked-read-round-trips\n   850\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\n   851\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\n   852\t        resources {:yin/s [:handle :s],\n   853\t                   :yin/c {:stream-id :yin/s, :cursor :kept-position}}\n   854\t        entry {:reason :next,\n   855\t               :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/c},\n   856\t               :stream-id :yin/s}\n   857\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! resources entry)]\n   858\t    (is (= {:yin.k/reason :next, :yin.k/cell :yin.k/c-0}\n   859\t           (:yin.k/pending lifted))\n   860\t        \"the cursor CELL id, S7.5.3 -- not a bare position\")\n   861\t    (is (= :kept-position\n   862\t           (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/position])))\n   863\t    (is (= #{:dao.stream.remote/v1}\n   864\t           (get-in lifted [:yin.k/requires :yin.k/cursor-profiles])))\n   865\t    (let [ctx {:segment 0, :pc 7, :env {}, :stack [], :k []}\n   866\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   867\t                                            (:yin.k/cells lifted) ctx)\n   868\t          e (:entry lowered)]\n   869\t      (is (= :next (:reason e)))\n   870\t      (is (= 7 (:pc e)) \"the registers ride the lower\")\n   871\t      (is (contains? (:resources lowered) (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id]))\n   872\t          \"the wait polls its own fresh cursor entry\")\n   873\t      (is (contains? (:resources lowered) (:stream-id e)))\n   874\t      (is (= :kept-position\n   875\t             (get-in lowered [:resources (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id])\n   876\t                              :cursor]))))))\n   877\t\n   878\t\n   879\t(deftest put-round-trips\n   880\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\n   881\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\n   882\t        resources {:yin/w [:handle :w]}\n   883\t        entry {:reason :put, :stream-id :yin/w, :datom \"hello\"}\n   884\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! resources entry)]\n   885\t    (is (= :put (get-in lifted [:yin.k/pending :yin.k/reason])))\n   886\t    (is (= \"hello\" (get-in lifted [:yin.k/pending :yin.k/value]))\n   887\t        \"the retained :datom -- a retry appends THIS\")\n   888\t    (is (empty? (:yin.k/cells lifted))\n   889\t        \"a put wait names a stream, never a cursor cell\")\n   890\t    (is (empty? (:yin.k/requires lifted)))\n   891\t    (let [ctx {:segment 0, :pc 3, :env {}, :stack [], :k []}\n   892\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   893\t                                            (:yin.k/cells lifted) ctx)\n   894\t          e (:entry lowered)]\n   895\t      (is (= :put (:reason e)))\n   896\t      (is (= \"hello\" (:datom e)))\n   897\t      (is (contains? (:resources lowered) (:stream-id e))\n   898\t          \"the target is a fresh reflection resource\"))))\n   899\t\n   900\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
