{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1790530211570-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice8-fixes-r4.glm-flash.report.md'","aggregated_output":"The ruling implemented verbatim** (collab/1790533100000-architect-ffi-migration-semantics.gpt-6-sol.findings.md), across the four allowed files:\n\n**1. RETAINED-CALL RESUME — carried pair, no receiver-handler fallback.** The lift now serves both endpoints: `lift-retained-request` (src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:328-368) mints `:yin.k/request` and `:yin.k/response` markers plus the kept response cell `:yin.k/response-cell` beside the verbatim envelope; either endpoint unservable refuses `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming that endpoint's identity (:352-361). `pending-markers` attaches both (:498-510). The lower refuses per endpoint at attach (lower-frame's `attach-all`, remote.cljc:513-524) and stamps the carried route on the lowered writer: `:stream-id req` (the request reflection's allocated key), `:response-cursor` (the response cell's allocated key), `:response-stream` (the response reflection's allocated key) (remote.cljc:625-647).\n\n**2. KEYS — collision-free batch allocation.** `lower-frame`/`lower-pending` gained an `occupied` parameter (the receiver's existing resource keys); each lowering allocates `:yin.k/k-N` keys — one per distinct served identity, one per distinct UCF cell id, same cell sharing within the batch, equal ids across frames differing — checked against `occupied`, `fixed-resource-keys` (the FFI pair + link pair, remote.cljc:478-483), and the batch, regenerating on collision (`fresh-key`, remote.cljc:485-495; allocation at remote.cljc:704-716). The response cursor resource lowers under the cell's allocated key with `:stream-id` = the response reflection's allocated key (`cell-resources`, remote.cljc:531-543); the resulting `:next` entry's `:cursor-ref :id` is that allocated key and its `:stream-id` names the response reflection (`lower-one`, remote.cljc:579-623).\n\n**3. THE SEMANTIC.CLJC DISPATCH.** `semantic-restore` now dispatches on carried route data: `carried-response-route` (src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:118-127) reads `[:response-cursor :response-stream]` off the writer, and the restored wait is re-keyed onto that carried route (:150-160) while `response-wait-entry`'s fixed defaults (:106-115) still serve ordinary writers.\n\n**4. TESTS pinned.** `a-retained-ffi-request-migrates-and-the-retry-resumes` (remote_test.cljc:509-618): both endpoint markers + verbatim envelope + kept cell at lift; the retry lands verbatim on the emitter's call-in through the carried request reflection (wire + mirror) and the emitter's bridge answers \"echo!\" there; the restored wait polls `:response-cursor`/`:response-stream` (asserted identical to `wait-a`'s `:cursor-ref`/`:stream-id`); the carried route's cursor advances; the receiver's own handler `{:op/echo \"local!\"}` answers only the subsequent call — its result is \"local!\" while the migrated result came from the emitter's pair — with the subsequent call's request/answer on the receiver's own pair. `retained-lift-refuses-when-an-endpoint-cannot-be-served` (:1135-1155): request and response refusals name each endpoint, no cell published. `retained-lower-refuses-when-an-endpoint-cannot-attach` (:1157-1180): refusal names the response identity; markers and cell survive in the UCF entry. `two-separately-lowered-frames-get-distinct-fresh-keys` (:1182-1227): equal `:yin.k/c-0` ids across batches get different keys, disjoint key sets, pre-held `:yin.k/k-10..12` regenerated away, every frame keeps a working kept-cursor entry. The old receiver-call-in expectation is replaced. Co-waiter sharing/independence pins remain in `shared-cursor-cells-lift-and-lower-shared`/`independent-cells-at-one-position-stay-independent` (updated to allocated keys). `semantic-restore-retained-response-route-test` (test/yin/vm/semantic_test.cljc:882-916): ordinary retained writers wait on the fixed keys; a lowered writer's restored wait polls its carried route.\n\n**Counts.**\n- Facade `yin.vm.ucf.remote-test` — JVM: 21 tests / 195 assertions, 0 failures 0 errors; Node: 21 / 195, 0 failures 0 errors; Dart (`flutter test`, freshly cljd-compiled): 21 of 21 passed.\n- `yin.vm.semantic-test` — JVM: 24 tests / 153 assertions, 0 failures 0 errors; Node: 24 / 153, 0 failures 0 errors; Dart: 24 of 24 passed.\n- Full JVM: 2277 tests / 183258 assertions — 1 failure, in `yin.repl.main-test` (main_test.cljc:675, the REPL served-stream peer check) — the concurrent slice-5 in-flight `yin.repl/*` work; both of my namespaces pass inside the same full run.\n- Hygiene: cljstyle check clean on all four files; clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings; added lines pure ASCII and ≤ 80 columns (the semantic.cljc:56 non-ASCII and the >80 lines at :76/:287/:531/:601/:688/:703/:854/:903 are pre-existing, outside my edits); no diagnostics; git shows exactly the four files (two untracked slice-8 files, two modified semantic files), no git operations performed.\n\nStatus: COMPLETE","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
