key module/link-request-resource\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:517:   {:handles {identity handle}}; `lower-frame` allocates each\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:589:   the carried response route (`:response-cursor`,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:590:   `:response-stream`) for its restore.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:642:                          :response-cursor\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:644:                          :response-stream resp})}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:674:(defn lower-frame\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:691:   (`:response-cursor`, `:response-stream`) for its restore.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:695:   (lower-frame attach! pendings cells contexts nil))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:733:   `lower-frame` gives. `occupied` is the receiver's existing\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:734:   resource keys, as `lower-frame`'s. Frame assembly that shares\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:735:   cursor entries across entries is `lower-frame`'s.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:739:   (let [r (lower-frame attach! [pending] cells [ctx] occupied)]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
