{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc | sed -n '1,45p;500,560p;905,1005p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.remote-test\n     2\t  \"The slice 8 acceptance row\n     3\t   (`docs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md` slice 8;\n     4\t   `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` S7.4.3, S7.5.3, S7.11.1\n     5\t   'Reflection acceptance'): a REAL machine parked through the engine\n     6\t   on a `:stream-next` wait migrates with a kept cursor and resumes\n     7\t   equivalently in a fresh engine state through a reflection; forced\n     8\t   eviction yields `gap` with the source's own recovery cursor; a\n     9\t   kept cursor that cannot survive the channel codec refuses the lift\n    10\t   before any cell is published; a source `serve!` refuses is\n    11\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied`; an `attach!` that answers gone is\n    12\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the stream at lower. Cursor cells are\n    13\t   minted and remapped across a whole frame set: two waiters on one\n    14\t   engine cell lift to one UCF cell and lower back shared, and\n    15\t   independent cells at one position stay independent (S7.5.3). The\n    16\t   remaining S7.4.3 variants -- `:put`, `:ffi`, `:ffi-request`,\n    17\t   `:link-request`, `:link-response`, `:install` -- round-trip\n    18\t   through stub `serve!`/`attach!` callbacks over the engine's own\n    19\t   wait-set shapes, since their proof is the shape of the bridge, not\n    20\t   the transport. The lowered waits the engine resolves at its own\n    21\t   fixed resource keys resume there for real: a retained\n    22\t   `:link-request` migrates and the engine's own poll retries it and\n    23\t   resumes on the response read at the fixed link keys; a retained\n    24\t   FFI request migrates, its retry appends at the fixed call-in key,\n    25\t   and the restored response wait -- `semantic-restore` parks it on\n    26\t   the receiver's fixed local call-out keys -- receives the retried\n    27\t   response the route cell carried.\"\n    28\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    29\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    30\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n    31\t            [dao.stream.remote :as remote]\n    32\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n    33\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    34\t            [yin.vm.linearize :as linearize]\n    35\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n    36\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n    37\t            [yin.vm.ucf.remote :as ucf.remote]))\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t;; =============================================================================\n    41\t;; The toy: two in-process ring buffers as the channel (as\n    42\t;; dao.stream.remote-test), with a served-table `serve!` on top\n    43\t;; =============================================================================\n    44\t\n    45\t(defn- ring\n   500\t        (is (= (:envelope entry) (:dao.stream/value r))\n   501\t            \"the envelope verbatim, appended via the fixed request key\"))\n   502\t      (let [done (vm/run receiver)]\n   503\t        (is (vm/halted? done))\n   504\t        (is (= 'host.the-module (vm/value done))\n   505\t            \"the require resumes with the module's own value\")\n   506\t        (is (empty? (:wait-set done)))))))\n   507\t\n   508\t\n   509\t(deftest a-retained-ffi-request-migrates-and-the-retry-resumes\n   510\t  (let [t (toy)\n   511\t        peer (served-peer t)\n   512\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t) #{:reader :writer})\n   513\t        attach! (attacher t)\n   514\t        program (then (call-node :op/echo \"hello\")\n   515\t                      (call-node :op/echo \"world\"))\n   516\t        [datoms parked entry call-in-src call-out-src]\n   517\t        (parked-caller program)\n   518\t        kept (get-in parked [:resources vm/call-out-cursor-key :cursor])\n   519\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! (:resources parked) entry)\n   520\t        pending (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   521\t        ;; the resumer's own pair and its own handler, under the fixed\n   522\t        ;; keys: they serve the program's subsequent calls and can\n   523\t        ;; never answer the migrated one\n   524\t        own-call-in (ring 8)\n   525\t        own-call-out (ring 8)\n   526\t        own (calling-machine own-call-in own-call-out\n   527\t                             {:op/echo (constantly \"local!\")})\n   528\t        own-pair (select-keys (:resources own)\n   529\t                              [vm/call-in-stream-key\n   530\t                               vm/call-out-stream-key\n   531\t                               vm/call-out-cursor-key])\n   532\t        lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! pending\n   533\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\n   534\t                                          (registers-of entry)\n   535\t                                          (keys own-pair))\n   536\t        e (:entry lowered)\n   537\t        rs (:resources lowered)\n   538\t        receiver (-> (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered own)\n   539\t                     (update :resources #(merge own-pair %)))\n   540\t        oldest (fn [h]\n   541\t                 (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h :dao.stream/oldest)))\n   542\t        ;; the emitter's bridge answered the migrated call before the\n   543\t        ;; migration: the response sits on the emitter's call-out,\n   544\t        ;; past the kept cursor\n   545\t        _ (stream/append! call-out-src\n   546\t                          (apply2/success-response\n   547\t                            (:call-id entry) \"echo!\"))\n   548\t        ;; phase 1: the sweep retries the retained request through the\n   549\t        ;; carried request reflection, and the restored response wait\n   550\t        ;; polls the carried response route\n   551\t        r1 (vm/run receiver)\n   552\t        wait-a (first (:wait-set r1))\n   553\t        warm-up (stream/next call-in-src (oldest call-in-src))\n   554\t        _ (serve-mirror! peer)\n   555\t        landed (stream/next call-in-src (oldest call-in-src))\n   556\t        ;; phase 2: the carried route delivers the response; the\n   557\t        ;; program's own next call parks on the receiver's local pair\n   558\t        ;; and its own handler answers it there\n   559\t        r2 (vm/run r1)]\n   560\t    (testing \"the machine parked through the engine, request retained\"\n   905\t                   :yin/call-out-cursor\n   906\t                   {:stream-id :yin/call-out, :cursor 5}}\n   907\t        entry {:reason :next, :call-id :call-7, :op :op/add,\n   908\t               :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :yin/call-out-cursor},\n   909\t               :stream-id :yin/call-out}\n   910\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! resources entry)\n   911\t        pending (:yin.k/pending lifted)]\n   912\t    (is (= :ffi (:yin.k/reason pending)))\n   913\t    (is (= :call-7 (:yin.k/call-id pending)))\n   914\t    (is (= :op/add (:yin.k/op pending)))\n   915\t    (is (= :yin.k/c-0 (:yin.k/cell pending)))\n   916\t    (is (= 5 (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/position]))\n   917\t        \"the response cell at its KEPT position\")\n   918\t    (let [ctx {:segment 0, :pc 9, :env {}, :stack [], :k []}\n   919\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! pending\n   920\t                                            (:yin.k/cells lifted) ctx)\n   921\t          e (:entry lowered)]\n   922\t      (is (= :next (:reason e)) \"the response wait is a :next waiter\")\n   923\t      (is (= :call-7 (:call-id e)))\n   924\t      (is (= :op/add (:op e)))\n   925\t      (is (contains? (:resources lowered) (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id]))\n   926\t          \"the response wait polls its own fresh cursor entry\")\n   927\t      (is (= 5 (get-in lowered [:resources (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id])\n   928\t                                :cursor]))))))\n   929\t\n   930\t\n   931\t(deftest ffi-retained-round-trips\n   932\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\n   933\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\n   934\t        envelope (apply2/request :call-7 :op/add [1 2])\n   935\t        resources {vm/call-in-stream-key [:handle :call-in],\n   936\t                   vm/call-out-stream-key [:handle :call-out],\n   937\t                   vm/call-out-cursor-key\n   938\t                   {:stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key, :cursor 2}}\n   939\t        entry {:reason :put, :request-sent true, :call-id :call-7,\n   940\t               :op :op/add, :stream-id vm/call-in-stream-key,\n   941\t               :datom envelope}\n   942\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! resources entry)\n   943\t        pending (:yin.k/pending lifted)]\n   944\t    (is (= :ffi-request (:yin.k/reason pending)))\n   945\t    (is (= :call-7 (:yin.k/call-id pending)))\n   946\t    (is (= :op/add (:yin.k/request-op pending)))\n   947\t    (is (= [1 2] (:yin.k/request-args pending)))\n   948\t    (is (contains? pending :yin.k/request))\n   949\t    (is (contains? pending :yin.k/response)\n   950\t        \"both endpoint markers ride beside the retained envelope\")\n   951\t    (is (= :yin.k/c-0 (:yin.k/response-cell pending))\n   952\t        \"the response route rides as a cell\")\n   953\t    (is (= (get-in pending [:yin.k/response :dao.stream/identity])\n   954\t           (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/stream\n   955\t                           :dao.stream/identity]))\n   956\t        \"the response endpoint's marker is the route cell's stream\")\n   957\t    (is (= 2 (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/position]))\n   958\t        \"the route cell at the emitter's kept call-out position\")\n   959\t    (is (= #{:dao.stream.remote/v1}\n   960\t           (get-in lifted [:yin.k/requires :yin.k/cursor-profiles]))\n   961\t        \"the frame carries a cursor profile: the route is a cell\")\n   962\t    (let [ctx {:segment 0, :pc 5, :env {}, :stack [], :k []}\n   963\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! pending\n   964\t                                            (:yin.k/cells lifted)\n   965\t                                            ctx\n   966\t                                            #{:yin.k/k-1 :yin.k/k-2})\n   967\t          e (:entry lowered)\n   968\t          rs (:resources lowered)]\n   969\t      (is (= :put (:reason e)))\n   970\t      (is (true? (:request-sent e)))\n   971\t      (is (= :call-7 (:call-id e)))\n   972\t      (is (= envelope (:datom e))\n   973\t          \"the envelope rebuilt verbatim under its call id\")\n   974\t      (is (contains? rs (:stream-id e))\n   975\t          \"the retry writes through the carried request reflection\")\n   976\t      (is (not= vm/call-in-stream-key (:stream-id e))\n   977\t          \"never the receiver's own call-in key\")\n   978\t      (is (not (contains? rs vm/call-in-stream-key)))\n   979\t      (is (not (contains? rs vm/call-out-stream-key)))\n   980\t      (is (not (contains? rs vm/call-out-cursor-key))\n   981\t          \"no route is ever installed at a fixed key\")\n   982\t      (is (not (contains? #{:yin.k/k-1 :yin.k/k-2}\n   983\t                          (:response-cursor e)))\n   984\t          \"occupied keys were regenerated away\")\n   985\t      (let [route (get rs (:response-cursor e))]\n   986\t        (is (some? route)\n   987\t            \"the response cell lowers under its own allocated key\")\n   988\t        (is (= 2 (:cursor route))\n   989\t            \"at the kept response position\")\n   990\t        (is (= (:response-stream e) (:stream-id route))\n   991\t            \"naming the carried response reflection\")\n   992\t        (is (contains? rs (:response-stream e))\n   993\t            \"which is attached\")\n   994\t        (is (not= vm/call-out-stream-key (:response-stream e))\n   995\t            \"never a fixed key\")))))\n   996\t\n   997\t\n   998\t(deftest link-request-round-trips\n   999\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\n  1000\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\n  1001\t        envelope {:yin.link/id [:t0 7], :yin.link/name 'foo,\n  1002\t                  :yin.link/format :yin.debruijn.code,\n  1003\t                  :yin.link/contract \"b2\"}\n  1004\t        resources {module/link-request-resource [:handle :req],\n  1005\t                   module/link-response-resource [:handle :resp]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '100,175p'\"","aggregated_output":"   100\t         :stack (or St [])\n   101\t         :env E\n   102\t         :k (if (seq K) K nil)\n   103\t         :halted? (and (not (:blocked? vm)) (nil? seg))))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(defn- response-wait-entry\n   107\t  \"The polling wait entry for a sent call awaiting its correlated response:\n   108\t   the machine registers {segment pc env stack k} plus the call-out reader\n   109\t   fields, in the shape `ffi/call-response-wait-entry` gives the walker.\"\n   110\t  [seg pc env stack k call-id]\n   111\t  {:segment seg, :pc pc, :env env, :stack stack, :k k,\n   112\t   :call-id call-id,\n   113\t   :reason :next,\n   114\t   :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id vm/call-out-cursor-key},\n   115\t   :stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key})\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\t(defn- carried-response-route\n   119\t  \"The response route a lowered retained writer carries -- its\n   120\t   [response cursor key, response stream key] pair, the route data\n   121\t   `yin.vm.ucf.remote` stamps on the lowered entry\n   122\t   (`yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` S7.4.3). nil when the\n   123\t   writer carries none: an ordinary retained call waits on the fixed\n   124\t   local call-out keys.\"\n   125\t  [entry]\n   126\t  (when (and (contains? entry :response-cursor)\n   127\t             (contains? entry :response-stream))\n   128\t    [(:response-cursor entry) (:response-stream entry)]))\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t(defn semantic-restore\n   132\t  \"Restore a wait-set or ready-queue entry into machine registers.\n   133\t\n   134\t   Two entry shapes carry more than registers:\n   135\t\n   136\t   - A `:request-sent` entry is a writer whose retained FFI request has now\n   137\t     been appended. The call starts waiting for its correlated response,\n   138\t     exactly as an immediately-sent one does, so the entry is replaced by its\n   139\t     response reader and the machine stays blocked. A writer carrying a\n   140\t     lowered call's response route (`:response-cursor`, `:response-stream`)\n   141\t     waits on that carried route; an ordinary one waits on the fixed local\n   142\t     call-out keys.\n   143\t   - A `:call-id` entry is a response reader. The woken value is a response\n   144\t     envelope, so `ffi/call-result` unwraps it, checks correlation, and the\n   145\t     parked call leaves `:parked` rather than accumulating.\"\n   146\t  ([base entry] (semantic-restore base entry (:value entry)))\n   147\t  ([base entry val]\n   148\t   (if (:request-sent entry)\n   149\t     (let [wait (response-wait-entry (:segment entry)\n   150\t                                     (:pc entry)\n   151\t                                     (:env entry)\n   152\t                                     (:stack entry)\n   153\t                                     (:k entry)\n   154\t                                     (:call-id entry))\n   155\t           wait (if-let [[cursor-key stream-key]\n   156\t                         (carried-response-route entry)]\n   157\t                  (assoc wait\n   158\t                         :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cursor-key}\n   159\t                         :stream-id stream-key)\n   160\t                  wait)]\n   161\t       (assoc base\n   162\t              :wait-set (conj (vec (or (:wait-set base) [])) wait)\n   163\t              :control nil\n   164\t              :k nil\n   165\t              :value :yin/blocked\n   166\t              :blocked? true\n   167\t              :halted? false))\n   168\t     (let [call-id (:call-id entry)\n   169\t           base (if call-id (update base :parked dissoc call-id) base)\n   170\t           val (if call-id (ffi/call-result val call-id) val)]\n   171\t       (put-registers base\n   172\t                      (:segment entry)\n   173\t                      (:pc entry)\n   174\t                      val\n   175\t                      (:stack entry)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-27 23:09:51 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-28 06:09:51 +07\n\n**P1 — The retained-call fix in the current tree does not match the requested retry path.** Lowering still sets the retained writer’s `:stream-id` to the *emitter’s request reflection* and adds a carried response route ([remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:625)). The integration test explicitly verifies that the retried request lands on the emitter’s call-in and that the migrated response comes from its call-out ([remote_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:548)). It therefore does not verify the specified receiver-local retry, receiver-local response, or `\"world!\"` result; it asserts `\"local!\"` ([remote_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:611)). This gate cannot sign off the stated structural fix.\n\nThe two former P1 mechanisms themselves are absent: response cells lower under allocated keys rather than fixed route keys ([remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:531)), and allocation avoids supplied occupied keys while sharing a key for the same cell within a batch ([remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:674)). I did not rerun the orchestrator’s suites.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\nSign-off: DENIED"}}
